{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1547095-rules-differences-between-the-different-systems","id":1547095,"title":"Rules differences between the different systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-12-17T00:20:24-08:00","id":1547095,"title":"Rules differences between the different systems","content":"I\u2019m sure this has been asked before, so I apologize if I missed it. What are the mechanical differences between nWoD and oWoD? I know VtR has blood potency while VtM has generations. I am somewhat familiar with nWoD, but very unfamiliar with oWoD. Would there be a way to convert a character from one to the other? Not just VtM/VtR, but CtD/CtL and some of the others as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24791-immortal","name":"Immortal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T01:11:01-08:00","id":1547098,"title":"","content":"CoD/nWoD: Fixed Target Number of 8, penalties subtract successes, heavily standardized Traits and powers.<br /> <br /> WoD: No fixed target number with a typical assumed TN of 6, penalties can alter any dimension of a roll, and Traits and powers are frequently heavily idiosyncratic or unique to some facet of the games where they're found - Vampire is pretty much the only game concerned about degeneration of characters as measured by Humanity, while Werewolf is much more aspirational and measures your ability to live up to a greater purpose via Renown, in addition to having some rough sort of power stats in Rage and Gnosis, the former is also their mechanical equivalent of Celerity. Mummies prior to M:tR, or at least the Shemsu-Heru, have a lot of different Traits measuring their soul states, which pretty much no one else does, and mummies from other cultural backgrounds can even differ markedly in what Traits they do have. It doesn't make for a smooth crossover experience, but was not a priority at the time, whereas expressing the needs and wants of the game was.<br /> <br /> WoD 5th Edition: Some unholy hybrid of the above that mostly just flattens everything out to make it work like Vampire in most mechanical capacities, which also ends up wildly distorting their themes. We don't have many games to compare as of yet, but those we do have tend to make the fans of other lines dread the release of the 5th edition version of their game.<br /> <br /> As for conversion between the pre-5th WoD and the CoD, there are conversion guides written to do so officially, though some material still gets left out (Rage was flat-out cut from Garou expressed through CoD terms). They're also written for 1e CoD (nWoD) rather than the 2e CoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T01:24:49-08:00","id":1547099,"title":"","content":"The differences range between the different gamelines (vampires are more similar, mummies are radically different) if there are even ones that share the same name. But especially with the Chronicles of Darkness 2nd Edition (the current one, which was re-titled from the nWoD to avoid have the same name for both), they have diverged even more mechanically from each other.<br /> <br /> At this point direct conversion from one to the other is basically impossible. It's not hard to transfer broad concepts (though it helps if they're not too pegged to specific game lore) as things are still close enough to be able to handle such ideas moving from one to the other, but specific existing characters? That's going to be a lot of work, if it even works out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T01:40:31-08:00","id":1547101,"title":"","content":"Penalties in CofD/nWoD subtract <i>dice,</i> not successes (and bonuses add them). The die target number is eight, which is rather high, but outside of combat and contested rolls, you only ever need to roll a single success, in contrast to how oWoD differentiates degrees of success, like how 1 success is a &quot;marginal success.&quot; In CofD, if you rolled a single 8, you didn't just scrape by, you succeeded. All the math is about how likely your dice pool is to roll an 8.<br /> <br /> nWoD/CofD is presented as a separate universe/setting/continuity from oWoD. While oWoD's Vampire: the Masquerade and CofD's Vampire: the Requiem are very similar in both themes and implementation, down to sharing a lot of their setting vocabulary, other CofD gamelines deviated farther thematically and conceptually. Changeling: the Dreaming, for example, is about people born with faerie souls in a world of dwindling wonder that threatens to choke the glamour from them. Changeling: the Lost is about people who were stolen away by the Fair Folk, were transformed by their time in glorious and terrible Faerie, and had to fight to claw their way back, to find a new place in a home that moved on without them while wondering when the Fair Folk's huntsmen will come for them to reclaim their escaped servants. A lot of concepts just won't easily translate.<br /> <br /> There are four official Translation Guides, each of which are based on the Revised Edition iteration of their respective oWoD game: Vampire the Masquerade and Vampire the Requiem, Werewolf the Apocalypse and Werewolf the Forsaken, Mage the Ascension and Mage the Awakening, and Demon the Fallen and Demon the Descent. The first three use the first edition of their respective CofD gameline, while Descent is a game that debuted after/alongside the CofD second edition ruleset. Each requires some tweaking and eyeballing, and rather than stopping at simply translating mechanics for one thing to another system, also discusses the differences between each gameline, both thematically and in setting specifics. For example, the Vampire Translation Guide talks about the difference between a Masquerade clan and a Requiem clan, and presents options for tweaking groups from one gameline to fit into the setting and mode of the other, such as Masquerade's Tremere Pyramid as a Requiem covenant. The Demon Translation Guide also discusses several setups for a game premise that could incorporate both distinct types of demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T17:02:57-08:00","id":1547121,"title":"","content":"Vampires are vampires, and Werewolves are werewolves, but they are so different in each setting that it is hard. The Mages from CoD however are so different from Mage the Ascension that I don't think it is possible to change one for another. However, the thing that is absolutely impossible is the conversion between Changeling the Lost and Changeling the Dream. Other than the name &quot;Changelings&quot;, they have NOTHING in common AT ALL. Totally different types of critters. It would be like trying to convert a Vampire into a Werewolf, or converting a Dragon into a Beholder (although I would even blink an eye if D&amp;D has created &quot;Beholder Dragons&quot; or &quot;Dragonite Beholder&quot;, but I digress). Not compatible at the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}